## 4. GITHUB FORKS

GitHub's Terms of Service grant GitHub users certain rights to fork public repositories through GitHub's platform functionality.

This license does not override those platform-level rights.

A GitHub fork does not grant permission to independently publish, redistribute, sell, or commercially exploit PyCraft or modified versions outside the rights granted by GitHub and this license.

## 5. CONTRIBUTIONS

Repository write access is granted to contributors who are invited and approved by the repository owner.

Authorized contributors may:
- Create and maintain their own branches in the official PyCraft repository.
- Submit pull requests for review.
- Participate in the development of the project.

Contributions must be submitted through pull requests.

A contribution is not accepted into the official project until an authorized maintainer reviews and merges it.

By submitting a contribution, you confirm that you have the right to submit it under these terms.

## 6. CONTRIBUTOR ACCESS MAINTENANCE

Every authorized contributor will receive an activity confirmation email once every 15 calendar days.

Each contributor must respond to the confirmation email within 15 calendar days of its delivery.

If a contributor does not respond within this period, their repository write access will be revoked as part of routine contributor access maintenance.

This procedure is an access cleanup measure, not a ban or permanent removal from the project.

The following conditions apply:
- Existing branches will be preserved.
- Previous commits and contributions will not be deleted.
- The contributor will retain access to the public repository.
- The contributor may request write access again at any time.
- Write access may be restored after the repository owner's approval.

Revoking write access does not constitute a ban and does not delete or invalidate previous contributions.

The purpose of this policy is to keep the contributor list active, organized, and maintainable.

